        "original_id": "c31e8ace-c1ba-5e66-9b1a-2f0d824afb68",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Craig Virgin, Chris Derrick, Lukas Verzbicas, James Munyala\n- Sports: Illinois Boys Cross Country, triathlon\n- Places: Illinois, Kaunas, Lithuania\n\nFacts:\n- In 1972, Craig Virgin ran 13:50.6 in Illinois Boys Cross Country and remains the record-holder.\n- In 2007, Chris Derrick ran 13:51.8, coming within five seconds of Craig Virgin’s Illinois Boys Cross Country record.\n- In 2010, Lukas Verzbicas ran 13:53.8, coming within five seconds of Craig Virgin’s Illinois Boys Cross Country record.\n- Lukas Verzbicas was born as Lukas Veržbickas on January 6, 1993, in Kaunas, Lithuania.\n- Lukas Verzbicas is a Lithuanian-American triathlete.\n- At the time, Craig Virgin suggested that these athletes displaced opportunities for American athletes.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6d0e891e-4048-51bb-be55-254cceb96c44",
        "text": "Page: Craig Virgin. Sentence: Additionally, Virgin remains the record-holder in Illinois Boys Cross Country, running a 13:50.6 in 1972, which has only been approached by within five seconds by Chris Derrick in 2007 (13:51.8) and Lukas Verzbicas in 2010 (13:53.8).\nPage: Lukas Verzbicas. Sentence: Lukas Verzbicas (born \"Lukas Veržbickas\" January 6, 1993 in Kaunas, Lithuania) is a Lithuanian-American triathlete.\nPage: James Munyala. Sentence: At the time, Craig Virgin suggested these athletes displaced opportunities for American athletes.",
